          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Ultracategories
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            endowed with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            meant to abstract the possibility of forming
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultraproducts"} ultraproducts
            %a{:href => "#Makkai87"} Makkai (1987)
            in order to prove
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conceptual+completeness"} strong conceptual completeness
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+logic"} coherent logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            of a coherent theory, on its own, is not sufficient to determine the theory up to any useful notion of equivalence, it becomes sufficient to reconstruct the theory up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
            once it is endowed with the structure of an ultracategory.
          %p
          #thm:makkai.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Makkai)
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Mod
